{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_mlbuwnd7srkz4h6o2z6kcg6t3nwmmzas3qo3ogvnsa557tjbbnya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeds. The remaining warning is about the private `State` enum being used in a `pub fn parse_instruction` signature, which I cannot fix without modifying either the enum definition or the function signature (both prohibited by rule #6).\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n- **`VCD::read_from_path`**: Opens the file and runs the dispatch loop from C — reading character-by-character and routing `$` instructions, `#` timestamps, expression characters (assignments), or whitespace.\n- **`VCD::get_signal_by_name`**: Linear scan over signals, comparing the null-terminated `name` slice against the requested name.\n- **`Signal::get_value_at_timestamp`**: Iterates value changes in order; returns the last change whose timestamp ≤ the queried timestamp (matching the \"previous_value\" walk in C).\n- **`parse_instruction`**: Implements all the C `fscanf` patterns manually with helper functions (`read_word`, `read_until_any`, `read_digits`, `skip_whitespace`). Handles `end`, `dumpvars`, `dumpall`, `scope` (with state transitions), `upscope`, `enddefinitions`, `comment`, `var` (skipping inner-module vars, otherwise pushing a new `Signal`), `date`, `version`, and `timescale`.\n- **`parse_timestamp`**: Reads optional whitespace + decimal digits, parses to `u32`.\n- **`parse_assignment`**: Reads the rest of the line; distinguishes vector (`b…` or other) vs scalar (`0`,`1`,`x`/`X`,`z`/`Z`) format. Splits into `value`/`signal_id`, ignores ids longer than one char, and appends to the signal's `value_changes` (using `strncpy`-style null-padded copy).\n- **`get_signal_index`**: Translates the first character to an offset from `'!'`, returning `None` if it's out of range.\n\nI also added small helper functions (`read_byte`, `unread_byte`, `read_word`, `read_until_any`, `read_digits`,